WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.943 --> 00:00:07.004
do former U.S.

2
00:00:07.064 --> 00:00:15.868
president Bill Clinton, TV talk-show host Oprah Winfrey, pop goddess Madonna, computer guru Bill Gates, and possibly your

3
00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:17.329
grandparents have in common?

4
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:25.313
They are all "baby boomers," people who were born after World War II, between 1946 and 1964.

5
00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:29.976
But these people are defined by more than just the years in which they were born.

6
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:37.805
Baby boomers are a generation that has both created and witnessed profound changes in the United States during

7
00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:39.586
a critical period in its history.

8
00:00:40.347 --> 00:00:46.330
After World War II, soldiers came home, and the Western world enjoyed a period of relative peace.

9
00:00:47.271 --> 00:00:52.895
Many countries created legislation to help returning soldiers reintegrate into society.

10
00:00:53.595 --> 00:01:00.080
In the United States, the government passed the Servicemen's Readjustment Act (more commonly known as the G.I.

11
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.802
Bill), which paid for war veterans to attend universities.

12
00:01:04.702 --> 00:01:10.305
Higher education led to better-paying jobs, which meant that couples could afford to have larger families.

13
00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:18.130
In addition, the bill provided low-interest home loans, which allowed many people to buy houses in the suburbs

14
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.611
to better accommodate their growing families.

15
00:01:21.592 --> 00:01:28.936
These rapidly developing suburbs caused a "building boom," as more houses, stores, schools, and shopping malls were constructed,

16
00:01:29.652 --> 00:01:33.975
creating dramatic changes in both the demographics and landscape of the nation.

17
00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:39.199
During the postwar era, there was a great emphasis on family and stability.

18
00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:43.382
Everyone's role in the family was clearly defined by society.

19
00:01:44.022 --> 00:01:45.503
The father worked in the office.

20
00:01:46.164 --> 00:01:48.205
The mother was a homemaker in the suburbs.

21
00:01:48.926 --> 00:01:50.547
The children did what they were told.

22
00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:57.452
This lifestyle is obvious in the seemingly perfect families of American TV shows like Leave It to Beaver,

23
00:01:58.036 --> 00:02:00.817
where the mother always wears a clean apron over her dress.

24
00:02:01.777 --> 00:02:04.738
But all of this changed in the tumultuous 1960s.

25
00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:11.880
One of the most important developments of this period was the availability of the birth control pill, often

26
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:18.122
simply called "the Pill," which allowed women to control the number of children they had.

27
00:02:18.282 --> 00:02:22.863
In 1964, a large drop in the birth rate signaled the end of the baby boom.

28
00:02:23.564 --> 00:02:28.478
At the same time, other sectors of society were experiencing drastic changes as well.

29
00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:36.343
In domestic politics, African Americans, led by Martin Luther King Jr., joined in mass demonstrations to demand equal

30
00:02:36.403 --> 00:02:40.825
civil rights, such as the right to vote and the right to a quality education.

31
00:02:41.446 --> 00:02:47.729
The decade was marked by the violent assassinations of leaders who had once brought hope to politics, such

32
00:02:47.809 --> 00:02:50.491
as Martin Luther King Jr., President John F.

33
00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:52.092
Kennedy, and his brother Robert.

34
00:02:52.604 --> 00:02:59.507
The presidency of Richard Nixon was plagued by the Watergate scandal, which made many Americans feel disillusioned and

35
00:02:59.627 --> 00:03:01.108
cynical about their government.

36
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:05.109
In the international arena, the cold war between the U.S.

37
00:03:05.229 --> 00:03:11.672
and the Soviet Union was intensifying, with the two countries competing against each other to develop their space

38
00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:17.615
programs, build larger stores of nuclear weapons, and increase their influence on other countries.

39
00:03:18.355 --> 00:03:18.895
The U.S.

40
00:03:18.955 --> 00:03:20.556
was embroiled in the Vietnam War.

41
00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:28.271
Thousands of young Americans became "draft dodgers" and avoided military service in what they thought was an immoral

42
00:03:28.311 --> 00:03:30.832
war by crossing the border into Canada.

43
00:03:31.472 --> 00:03:38.595
Finally, in 1975, the last American troops withdrew from Vietnam, bringing about the end of the war and

44
00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:41.076
closing this period of political unrest.

45
00:03:41.896 --> 00:03:47.098
On the social level, the Pill and the rise of feminism led to an increase in the number

46
00:03:47.138 --> 00:03:50.560
of women leaving the home in order to pursue their own careers.

47
00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:57.466
The financial independence of women also led to a rise in divorce, which became less scandalous and more

48
00:03:57.506 --> 00:04:04.328
accepted. Meanwhile, in the world of music, rock and roll and its rebellious attitude were shaping the young

49
00:04:04.368 --> 00:04:08.369
generation, whose motto was "don't trust anyone over thirty."

50
00:04:09.129 --> 00:04:14.731
They held festivals such as Woodstock, where they listened to rock music for days and proved that their

51
00:04:14.771 --> 00:04:19.272
reputation for being antiestablishment and antirules was well deserved.

52
00:04:20.496 --> 00:04:28.140
Many young people became long-haired "hippies," refusing to conform to society's norms and seeking liberation from its restrictions.

53
00:04:29.041 --> 00:04:32.363
They saw their parents as slaves to a materialistic lifestyle.

54
00:04:33.103 --> 00:04:37.625
Instead of joining the workforce, many hippies lived together in cooperative communities.

55
00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:44.209
They preferred to go back to nature; the men grew long hair and beards, the women wore free-flowing,

56
00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:49.312
long dresses that they often made themselves, and many of them ate vegetarian diets.

57
00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.477
They promoted peace and love.

58
00:04:51.978 --> 00:04:55.220
They also often experimented with Eastern religions and drugs.

59
00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:59.164
By this time, each household had its own TV set.

60
00:04:59.664 --> 00:05:04.888
The baby boom generation was the first to grow up watching the world on "the box," as television

61
00:05:04.928 --> 00:05:05.829
was often called.

62
00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:11.314
Of course, the advertising industry would not let an opportunity like this pass by.

63
00:05:12.094 --> 00:05:17.459
Companies used TV to promote their products, and the economy, as a result, grew in the direction of

64
00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:18.880
the whims of the baby boomers.

65
00:05:20.008 --> 00:05:26.692
In the United States alone, the baby boom generation makes up 77 million people, which is about 28

66
00:05:26.732 --> 00:05:28.153
percent of the population!

67
00:05:29.053 --> 00:05:34.877
Just by their sheer numbers, the boomers are the movers and shakers who form contemporary society.

68
00:05:35.697 --> 00:05:40.440
In fact, the Baby Boomer Headquarters Web site boasts, "We are the economy."

69
00:05:41.141 --> 00:05:45.303
It is true that the majority of those working right now are part of this generation.

70
00:05:45.964 --> 00:05:50.447
Furthermore, most of the decision-makers in society today are of this generation.

71
00:05:51.268 --> 00:05:57.333
Most experts agree that baby boomers will be in positions of control in government and industry until the

72
00:05:57.393 --> 00:06:04.439
2020s. Another example of the continuing influence of this generation is the growing market for beauty and health

73
00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:09.844
products, cosmetic surgery, and other services to preserve youth and delay aging.

74
00:06:10.665 --> 00:06:17.250
No one can deny that the multibillion-dollar fitness industry got a huge push from another baby boomer, Jane

75
00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:23.395
Fonda. She set the trend for other boomers by promoting exercise as a way to remain young.

76
00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:28.500
Consumerism in general saw a significant increase in this generation.

77
00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:35.125
Unlike the grandparents of the baby boomers, who lived during the Great Depression and were cautious about spending,

78
00:06:35.706 --> 00:06:39.008
the baby boomers enjoyed a time of relative peace and prosperity.

79
00:06:39.829 --> 00:06:43.232
This affluence encouraged the boomers to become lavish consumers.

80
00:06:44.164 --> 00:06:49.286
As the baby boomers begin to retire, the changes in countries' economies will be enormous.

81
00:06:49.947 --> 00:06:53.548
First of all, the workforce will lose many of its most-skilled members.

82
00:06:54.148 --> 00:06:59.771
Moreover, the cost to pension funds and social-security systems will increase astronomically.

83
00:07:00.511 --> 00:07:04.413
Some predict that the burden will be too great for the economy and cause it to suffer.

84
00:07:05.093 --> 00:07:10.275
There are concerns, too, that the health-care system will not be able to deal with the vast population

85
00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:14.430
of senior citizens, who will need more medical attention at the end of their lives.

86
00:07:15.571 --> 00:07:20.975
These issues have prompted many to try to find a way to provide for this aging generation without

87
00:07:21.035 --> 00:07:24.537
damaging the economy, but a solution has not yet been found.

88
00:07:25.217 --> 00:07:29.801
There is no doubt the baby boomers' economic impact will be felt for many years to come.

89
00:07:30.461 --> 00:07:35.585
Strangely enough, it is not the boomers' effect on the economy that has had the greatest influence on

90
00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:41.553
modern life; rather, it is the social norms that have been, in many cases, totally reversed due to

91
00:07:41.573 --> 00:07:42.213
their choices.

92
00:07:43.073 --> 00:07:48.255
They have demonstrated the power that groups have when they work together to push for political or social

93
00:07:48.315 --> 00:07:55.818
change. Their attitudes have shaped the way future generations view politics, social norms, and even the natural process

94
00:07:55.858 --> 00:07:56.419
of aging.

95
00:07:57.099 --> 00:08:01.981
Women of this generation have gained greater and greater financial stature and political power.

96
00:08:02.721 --> 00:08:07.883
Above all, the baby boomers have helped create a society of people that will not accept at face

97
00:08:07.923 --> 00:08:09.824
value what is placed in front of them.

98
00:08:10.577 --> 00:08:12.924
Rather than accept the rules, they make their own.
